":1,"detail":"流動比率 = 10.49"},{"id":7,"category":"槓桿與償債","desc":"股本未遭稀釋 (ΔShares ≤ 0)","passed":1,"detail":"未大幅增發新股割韭菜"},{"id":8,"category":"營運效率","desc":"毛利率擴張 (ΔMargin > 0)","passed":1,"detail":"產品定價權增強，毛利結構健康"},{"id":9,"category":"營運效率","desc":"資產週轉率提升 (ΔTurnover > 0)","passed":1,"detail":"每單位資產產出效益改善"}],"fair_val":64.73,"default_fair_val":64.73,"premium_pct":133.3,"is_undervalued":false,"pe_trailing":33.3,"pe_forward":29.3,"pb_trailing":8.8,"pb_forward":7.9,"div_yield":0,"ps_ratio":7.1,"fcf_to_ev":10.51,"fcf_to_mcap":3.51,"liab_to_assets":9.6,"cash_to_assets":76.6,"current_ratio":10.49,"roe":26.5,"roa":24,"moat":{"ticker":"RDDT","period":"2026Q2","m1_brand_pricing":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"Reddit 擁有強大的品牌認知度，其社群文化和用戶生成內容形成了獨特的品牌資產。然而，其定價權相對有限，主要依賴廣告收入，且用戶對廣告的容忍度存在上限。雖然品牌能吸引用戶和廣告商，但直接轉化為高定價能力仍有挑戰，尤其是在面對其他數位廣告平台競爭時。品牌價值主要體現在用戶黏性和活躍度上，而非直接的價格提升能力。","comment_en":"Reddit possesses strong brand recognition, with its community culture and user-generated content forming a unique brand asset. However, its pricing power is relatively limited, primarily relying on advertising revenue, and user tolerance for ads has its limits. While the brand attracts users and advertisers, directly translating this into high pricing power remains a challenge, especially when competing with other digital advertising platforms. The brand's value is mainly reflected in user engagement and activity, rather than direct price increase capabilities."},"m2_patents_regulatory":{"score":2,"comment_zh":"Reddit 的核心業務模式高度依賴開放的社群互動和內容分享，這類業務較難透過專利或嚴格的監管壁壘來保護。其技術優勢更多體現在平台運營和演算法上，但這些並非傳統意義上的專利壁壘。監管風險（如內容審核、數據隱私）是其面臨的挑戰，而非保護其競爭優勢的工具。因此，在專利和監管方面，Reddit 的護城河非常薄弱。","comment_en":"Reddit's core business model relies heavily on open community interaction and content sharing, making it difficult to protect through patents or strict regulatory barriers. Its technological advantages lie more in platform operations and algorithms, which are not traditional patent moats. Regulatory risks (e.g., content moderation, data privacy) are challenges rather than tools to protect its competitive advantages. Therefore, Reddit's moat in patents and regulation is very weak."},"m3_high_switching_costs":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"Reddit 的用戶轉換成本相對較低，用戶可以輕易地在不同社群平台間切換。然而，對於深度參與的用戶和社群管理者而言，他們在 Reddit 上投入的時間、建立的聲譽和連結網絡構成了隱性的轉換成本。這些用戶可能因為習慣、社群歸屬感或已建立的網絡而不願輕易離開。但這並非嚴格的技術或合約鎖定，轉換成本的強度有待加強。","comment_en":"User switching costs on Reddit are relatively low, as users can easily move between different community platforms. However, for deeply engaged users and community moderators, the time invested, reputation built, and network connections on Reddit constitute implicit switching costs. These users may be reluctant to leave due to habit, sense of community belonging, or established networks. This is not a strict technical or contractual lock-in, and the strength of switching costs needs further reinforcement."},"m4_network_effects":{"score":9,"comment_zh":"Reddit 的網絡效應極為顯著。越多的用戶加入，平台上的內容就越豐富、越多元，討論也越活躍，這反過來吸引更多用戶。活躍的社群和子版塊（subreddits）形成了獨特的生態系統，用戶在這裡找到歸屬感和興趣點，使得平台對新用戶和現有用戶都極具吸引力。這種正向循環是其核心競爭優勢，難以被複製。","comment_en":"Reddit's network effects are extremely significant. The more users join, the richer and more diverse the content on the platform becomes, and discussions are more active, which in turn attracts more users. Active communities and subreddits form a unique ecosystem where users find belonging and points of interest, making the platform highly attractive to both new and existing users. This positive feedback loop is its core competitive advantage and is difficult to replicate."},"m5_cost_advantage_scale":{"score":5,"comment_zh":"Reddit 作為一個大型社群平台，在獲取用戶和內容方面具有一定的規模優勢，能夠攤薄內容生產和基礎設施的成本。然而，其商業模式主要依賴廣告，與 Google、Meta 等巨頭相比，在廣告技術和數據分析方面的規模經濟效應仍有差距。雖然用戶基數龐大，但將此轉化為顯著的成本優勢以壓制競爭對手，仍需進一步發展。","comment_en":"As a large community platform, Reddit has a certain scale advantage in user and content acquisition, allowing it to spread the costs of content production and infrastructure. However, its business model relies mainly on advertising, and compared to giants like Google and Meta, there is still a gap in the economies of scale in ad technology and data analytics. Despite its massive user base, further development is needed to translate this into a significant cost advantage to suppress competitors."},"m6_unique_geography_assets":{"score":2,"comment_zh":"Reddit 的業務模式是全球化的，其內容和用戶基礎遍布世界各地，並無明顯的地理區域性優勢。雖然在特定國家或地區可能擁有較高的用戶滲透率，但這更多是網絡效應的體現，而非獨特的地理資產。其核心價值在於其全球性的社群網絡，而非特定地點的資源或市場。","comment_en":"Reddit's business model is global, with its content and user base spread across the world, lacking distinct geographical advantages. While it may have high user penetration in specific countries or regions, this is more a manifestation of network effects rather than unique geographical assets. Its core value lies in its global community network, not resources or markets in specific locations."},"m7_operational_efficiency":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"Reddit 在管理龐大用戶群體和海量 UGC 內容方面展現了相當的運營效率。其平台架構能夠支持高併發訪問和內容分發。儘管面臨內容審核的挑戰，但其通過社群自律和演算法推薦，在維持平台活躍度和秩序方面做得不錯。持續的技術投入和優化是其運營效率的關鍵，使其能夠在規模擴張的同時保持相對穩定的用戶體驗。","comment_en":"Reddit demonstrates considerable operational efficiency in managing its vast user base and massive UGC content. Its platform architecture supports high concurrency and content distribution. Despite content moderation challenges, it has performed well in maintaining platform activity and order through community self-regulation and algorithmic recommendations. Continuous technological investment and optimization are key to its operational efficiency, enabling it to maintain a relatively stable user experience while scaling."},"m8_capital_allocation":{"score":7,"comment_zh":"Reddit 的財務狀況顯示出良好的現金流和較低的負債，為其資本配置提供了彈性。公司近年來積極探索多元化收入來源，包括廣告、付費會員和數據授權，顯示出管理層在尋求長期價值增長方面的努力。雖然過去的 IPO 歷史和盈利能力有待觀察，但其穩健的資產負債表和對新業務的探索，預示著其在資本配置上具有一定的潛力，以支持未來的發展。","comment_en":"Reddit's financial health indicates strong cash flow and low debt, providing flexibility for capital allocation. The company has actively explored diversified revenue streams, including advertising, premium memberships, and data licensing, demonstrating management's efforts to seek long-term value growth. While its past IPO history and profitability are subject to observation, its solid balance sheet and exploration of new ventures suggest potential in capital allocation to support future development."},"m9_customer_retention":{"score":8,"comment_zh":"Reddit 在用戶留存方面表現出色，這得益於其強大的社群黏性和網絡效應。用戶在平台上找到歸屬感、獲取資訊、參與討論，形成了高度的用戶忠誠度。子版塊（subreddits）的深度和廣度滿足了用戶多樣化的需求，使得用戶一旦融入，便難以離開。這種基於興趣和社群的連結，是 Reddit 維持高用戶活躍度和留存率的關鍵。","comment_en":"Reddit excels in user retention, thanks to its strong community stickiness and network effects. Users find belonging, information, and participate in discussions on the platform, fostering high user loyalty. The depth and breadth of subreddits cater to diverse user needs, making it difficult for users to leave once integrated. This connection based on interests and community is key to Reddit's high user activity and retention rates."},"m10_durability":{"score":6,"comment_zh":"Reddit 的商業模式具有一定的持久性，其 UGC 內容生產模式能夠持續不斷地產生新鮮內容，滿足用戶需求。然而，其對廣告收入的依賴以及社群平台面臨的內容審核、用戶行為變化等挑戰，也帶來了不確定性。與傳統的特許經營權或擁有稀缺資產的公司相比，Reddit 的持久性更多地取決於其持續吸引和留存用戶的能力，以及適應不斷變化的互聯網環境。","comment_en":"Reddit's business model has a degree of durability, with its UGC content production model continuously generating fresh content to meet user needs. However, its reliance on advertising revenue and challenges faced by community platforms, such as content moderation and changing user behaviors, also bring uncertainty. Compared to traditional franchises or companies with scarce assets, Reddit's durability depends more on its ability to continuously attract and retain users and adapt to the ever-changing internet landscape."},"overall_moat_verdict_zh":"Reddit 的護城河主要建立在其強大的網絡效應和用戶留存能力之上，形成了一種獨特的社群生態系統。其品牌價值吸引了大量用戶和內容創作者，構成了難以撼動的用戶基礎。然而，在定價權、專利監管和規模成本方面，其護城河相對較弱，尤其是在面對科技巨頭的廣告競爭時。Reddit 更像是一個擁有龐大用戶流量的「收費橋」或「內容集散地」，其價值在於連接用戶與資訊，並從中獲取廣告收益。其持久性取決於能否持續維持社群活力並有效轉化流量為利潤，同時應對潛在的監管和競爭壓力。","overall_moat_verdict_en":"Reddit's moat is primarily built upon its powerful network effects and user retention capabilities, forming a unique community ecosystem. Its brand value attracts a large number of users and content creators, constituting a formidable user base. However, its moat is relatively weaker in pricing power, patents/regulation, and cost advantages, especially when competing for advertising revenue against tech giants. Reddit functions more like a 'toll bridge' or 'content hub' with massive user traffic, deriving value from connecting users with information and monetizing through advertising. Its durability hinges on sustaining community vitality and effectively converting traffic into profit while navigating potential regulatory and competitive pressures.","evidenceHash":"de8e9fecfd1305f260b7841feb1c08c84dc74c26e98c024a1a60318fa7ba19ff","assessmentPolicy":"us-buffett-moat-v3"},"ratingSources":{"moat":{"reason":null},"fScore":{"score":9,"checkedAt":null},"zScore":{"asOfDate":"2025-12-31","period":"FY 2025","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":"z","zone":"superRobust","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-27T16:12:46.364Z","evidenceHash":"340d5b86cee29b1b7537ce314a0d53a065855482d88c9a4f6da522165d2cf120"},"mScore":{"asOfDate":"2025-12-31","period":"FY 2025","basis":"comparableAnnual","model":null,"zone":"clean","reason":null,"scoringCurrency":"USD","applicability":null,"checkedAt":"2026-10-27T16:12:46.364Z","evidenceHash":"340d5b86cee29b1b7537ce314a0d53a065855482d88c9a4f6da522165d2cf120"}},"fin_valuation":{"is_financial":false},"image":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/RDDT.png","logo":"https://images.financialmodelingprep.com/symbol/RDDT.png","website":"https://www.redditinc.com","ceo":"Steven Ladd Huffman","full_time_employees":"2555","description":"Reddit, Inc. oversees an internet-based service dedicated to fostering diverse online communities. This platform categorizes groups by shared passions, enabling its users to participate in dialogues through recounting experiences, sharing external web addresses, uploading visual and video content, and engaging in direct replies. Founded in 2005, the corporation maintains its central operations in San Francisco, California. Reddit, Inc. also functions as a controlled subsidiary of Advance Publications, Inc.","description_en":"Reddit, Inc. oversees an internet-based service dedicated to fostering diverse online communities. This platform categorizes groups by shared passions, enabling its users to participate in dialogues through recounting experiences, sharing external web addresses, uploading visual and video content, and engaging in direct replies. Founded in 2005, the corporation maintains its central operations in San Francisco, California. Reddit, Inc. also functions as a controlled subsidiary of Advance Publications, Inc.","description_zh":"**Reddit, Inc. (RDDT) 業務營運概述**\n\nReddit, Inc. 是一家營運基於網際網路的社群平台公司，致力於建立多元化的線上社群。該平台透過匯集擁有共同興趣的使用者，形成各式各樣的「看板」（subreddits），讓使用者得以透過分享個人經驗、外部連結、圖文影音內容，以及直接回覆等方式進行深度交流與討論。\n\nReddit 的核心營運模式為內容驅動的社群互動，並透過廣告業務獲利。其關鍵技術在於強大的內容分級、搜尋與推薦演算法，以維持使用者參與度和平台活躍度。公司成立於 2005 年，總部位於美國加州舊金山，並為 Advance Publications, Inc. 的控股子公司。Reddit 透過其龐大的使用者基礎與活躍的社群生態，成為重要的線上資訊交流與意見匯集平台。","address":"South Tower","city":"San Francisco","state":"CA","zip":"94107","country":"US","phone":"(415) 494-8016","full_address":"South Tower, San Francisco, CA 94107, US","range_52w":"119.27-263.5","year_high":263.5,"year_low":119.27,"all_time_high":0,"all_time_low":119.27,"inst_ownership_pct":null,"insider_ownership_pct":null,"top_holders":[],"insider_trades":[{"date":"2026-10-16","name":"Wong Jennifer L.","title":"officer: Chief Operating Officer","is_buy":null,"action":"M-Exempt","shares":14563,"price":25.29,"total_val":0.37},{"date":"2026-10-16","name":"Wong Jennifer L.","title":"officer: Chief Operating Officer","is_buy":null,"action":"M-Exempt","shares":14563,"price":25.29,"t